## ⚠️ Critical Proxy-Target & Scope Caveats

1. **Near rule-based labelling.** `Late_delivery_risk` is a pre-computed label in the DataCo dataset that heavily reflects near rule-based dispatch logic rather than real courier variance. For Same Day orders, the order hour alone separates outcomes: orders placed before 12:00 are late {{ M.same_day_noon_rule.late_rate_before_noon | pct1 }} of the time, orders from 12:00 onward {{ M.same_day_noon_rule.late_rate_from_noon | pct1 }} ({{ M.same_day_noon_rule.orders | int }} Same Day orders).
2. **Standard Class has almost no signal.** Standard Class is {{ M.per_mode[mode=Standard Class].share | pct1 }} of test orders, and the model's ROC-AUC there is **{{ M.per_mode[mode=Standard Class].roc_auc | f4 }}** (95% CI {{ M.per_mode[mode=Standard Class].roc_auc_ci_lo | f4 }} to {{ M.per_mode[mode=Standard Class].roc_auc_ci_hi | f4 }}; signal: **{{ M.per_mode[mode=Standard Class].flag | raw }}**). The aggregate test ROC-AUC ({{ M.test.roc_auc | f4 }}) is driven by First Class ({{ M.per_mode[mode=First Class].roc_auc | f4 }}) and Same Day ({{ M.per_mode[mode=Same Day].roc_auc | f4 }}). A model trained on Standard Class alone reaches only {{ M.verification.segment_models.Standard Class.segment_model_roc_auc | f4 }}.
3. **The payment-type (TRANSFER) effect is a labelling artifact.** All {{ M.verification.cancel_fraud_orders | int }} CANCELED / SUSPECTED_FRAUD orders are TRANSFER payments and every one of them carries `Late_delivery_risk = 0`. Within each shipping mode the TRANSFER late rate differs from other payment types by {{ M.verification.transfer_gap_within_mode_all | pp1 }}; with those orders removed the difference is {{ M.verification.transfer_gap_within_mode_clean | pp1 }}. Do not read TRANSFER as lower payment risk.
4. **Not validated on Indian D2C.** This dataset represents global supply chain orders (predominantly North America and LATAM). It does not capture Indian D2C last-mile dynamics (NDR verification, fake door attempts, PIN-code delivery tiers, or COD payment fraud). Do not deploy without retraining on actual courier and return telemetry.
5. **Scores are clustered.** The calibrated score takes only {{ M.score_clusters.unique_scores_test | int }} distinct values on the test set; {{ M.score_clusters.largest_standard_cluster_share_of_standard | pct1 }} of Standard Class orders share one score. Cutoffs are therefore placed in low-density gaps between clusters (see Risk tiers).

